{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"ecosystem/inference-providers","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Inference Providers","words":1070,"objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Say what an inference provider is, and what a gateway adds","Know when going straight to the model's maker makes sense","Use a checklist beyond price, including what happens to your data"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[{"key":"ecosystem/agent-frameworks","number":35,"title":"Agent Frameworks","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"ecosystem/agent-frameworks","number":35,"title":"Agent Frameworks","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"ecosystem/inference-engines","number":37,"title":"Inference Engines","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"the-gateway-router","text":"The Gateway (Router)","depth":2},{"id":"inference-from-llm-vendors","text":"Inference from LLM Vendors","depth":2},{"id":"what-to-compare-beyond-the-price","text":"What to Compare, Beyond the Price","depth":2},{"id":"starting-for-free","text":"Starting for Free","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"️-tools","text":"🛠️ Tools","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":" showed that running a model is called inference, and that you can do it in the cloud. This module is about the companies that sell that service, and what to compare when you choose one."}],"lead":true},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"inference provider"}]},{"type":"text","text":" runs AI models on its own computers and rents you access to them. You send text, you get text back, and you pay for how much text went through, counted in tokens. You own none of the machines. It is like paying for electricity by use instead of owning a power plant."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"If your company buys AI access, someone has to choose a provider, and the price per token is the number everyone quotes. This module gives you the questions that matter more, especially the one about where your data goes."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-gateway-router","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Gateway (Router)"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://openrouter.ai/"},"inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/openrouter-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"gateway"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (also called a router). It sits in front of many providers, so you use one account, one bill and one way of connecting, and you can reach almost any model."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"You can switch models by changing one line."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If a better model comes out on Monday, you can use it a few hours later."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"One account instead of many."}]}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Failover:"}]},{"type":"text","text":" if one provider is down, the request can go to another one instead of failing."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The same model from several sellers"}]},{"type":"text","text":", at different prices and speeds, so you can choose."}]}]}]},{"type":"image","number":"36.1","title":"One API, Many Models","note":"One door in the middle, many models on one side and many builders on the other. The bottom strip shows how the gateway itself makes money: it builds no model of its own, so it earns whichever model wins, and people who build through it tend to stay.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/openrouter-gateway.webp","alt":"One API, Many Models","width":1400,"height":933},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The cost is one more company between you and the model, and a tiny delay."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/portkey.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Portkey"}]},{"type":"text","text":" does the same routing job with your own accounts, and adds things a company team asks for: guards, traces, budget limits and caching."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A warning about a different kind of router: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/agentrouter.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"AgentRouter"}]},{"type":"text","text":" gives one wallet for many paid services an agent might use, such as email, phone and travel booking. It holds your money and sees every call you send through it, and its website does not say which company runs it. Treat it like any third party that handles your data."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"inference-from-llm-vendors","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Inference from LLM Vendors"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The other way is to buy directly from the company that made the model: "},{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/openai-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"OpenAI, "},{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/anthropic-mono.svg","alt":"","mono":true},{"type":"text","text":"Anthropic or "},{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/google.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Google. You get their newest models first, and features only they offer, such as cheaper repeated instructions (caching), discounts for big batches, and higher limits."}]},{"type":"image","number":"36.2","title":"Claude Price List","note":"Anthropic's own price list. The first time you store repeated instructions costs a little more than normal, and every reuse after that costs only a small fraction. That is caching in plain terms.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/anthropic-pricing.webp","alt":"Claude Price List","width":974,"height":674},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Many companies do both: they buy directly for the model they use every day, and use a gateway to try everything else."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-to-compare-beyond-the-price","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What to Compare, Beyond the Price"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The price per million tokens is the number everyone quotes, and it is the worst number to decide on by itself."}]},{"type":"image","number":"36.3","title":"OpenRouter Model List","note":"OpenRouter's own list of models. Price is only two of the columns: the same row also shows how much text fits in one request, how fast the first word arrives and how fast the answer streams. Some models appear twice, and the cheaper batch copy is for work that can wait.","src":"course-images/ecosystem/openrouter-models.webp","alt":"OpenRouter Model List","width":1577,"height":735},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is a buyer's checklist:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Caching."}]},{"type":"text","text":" If your assistant sends the same long instructions with every request, a provider that caches them charges much less for each repeat. This can matter more than the base price."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Rate limits."}]},{"type":"text","text":" How many requests per minute you are allowed. A good price does not help if your requests wait in a queue."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Speed, and which kind."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The time until the first word appears is what a person feels in a chat. The total time is what a big batch job feels. These are different numbers."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Limits on size."}]},{"type":"text","text":" How much text fits in one request, and how long one answer can be. The answer limit is the one people forget, until a long answer gets cut off."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What happens to your data."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Does the provider keep your text? For how long? Can it use your text to train its models? If your requests contain customer or employee data, read this part before you send anything. For HR, finance and legal work, this question comes first."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quality from different sellers."}]},{"type":"text","text":" Through a gateway, two sellers can offer a model with the same name, but one may run a shrunk, lower-quality copy (the quantization from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":") to be cheaper."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"starting-for-free","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Starting for Free"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://aistudio.google.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"logo","src":"course-images/ecosystem/logos/google.svg","alt":"","mono":false},{"type":"text","text":"Google AI Studio"}]}]},{"type":"text","text":" and OpenRouter both have free plans with daily limits, enough to learn on and to test an idea."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"One warning. A free plan tells you whether a model "},{"type":"emphasis","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"can"}]},{"type":"text","text":" do your task. It does not tell you how fast your product will feel, because free capacity is slower, more limited, and the first to be cut when the provider is busy. Test speed on the plan you will actually pay for."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Inference provider"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a company that runs AI models and rents access per token."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Gateway"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (router): one door to many models and providers."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Failover"}]},{"type":"text","text":": moving a request to another provider when one is down."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Caching"}]},{"type":"text","text":": paying less for instructions you send again and again."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Rate limit"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how many requests you may send per minute."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Data retention"}]},{"type":"text","text":": whether and how long a provider keeps your text."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Inference providers rent you AI models by the token. A gateway like OpenRouter gives you one door to many of them; going straight to the maker gives you their newest models and special features. Do not choose on price alone: check caching, limits, speed, answer length, quality, and above all what happens to your data."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": What does a gateway give you that a single provider does not? And which question on the checklist matters most when your requests contain employee data?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🛠️ Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://openrouter.ai/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenRouter"}]},{"type":"text","text":": one account for many models, and the fastest way to compare them"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://portkey.ai/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Portkey"}]},{"type":"text","text":": routing with your own accounts, plus guards and traces"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://aistudio.google.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Google AI Studio"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a free plan with a daily allowance, enough to learn on"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":[{"question":"What does an inference provider sell you?","options":["A copy of the model weights to run on your own machines","The machines, so that you can host the model yourself","Access to a model that runs on their hardware, paid per token","One fixed monthly price for unlimited calls to one model"],"answer":2,"explain":"The provider runs the model on its own hardware, and you pay per token. You own none of the machines and none of the weights."},{"question":"A gateway such as OpenRouter gives you one key for many models. What is the cost?","options":["One extra hop through another company's infrastructure","A separate account and rate limit for each vendor","No failover when one provider has an outage","Only one seller for each open-weights model"],"answer":0,"explain":"Your request goes through another company's infrastructure, which adds a little latency. Separate accounts for each vendor are what a gateway removes."},{"question":"Why does a team go direct to the model maker, such as OpenAI, Anthropic or Google?","options":["To use one key and one API shape for many models","To choose between several sellers of one open-weights model","To move each request to another provider during an outage","To get features only the maker ships, such as prompt caching"],"answer":3,"explain":"The maker usually ships new models first, and it offers prompt caching, batch discounts and higher rate limits. One key for many models is what a gateway gives you."},{"question":"Your agent sends the same long system prompt on every turn. Which line of a provider's pricing page matters most?","options":["The price per million tokens","Prompt caching for the repeated prompt","The size of the context window","The daily limit of the free tier"],"answer":1,"explain":"A provider that caches a long, stable prompt charges a fraction for each repeat. The price per token alone is the worst number to decide on."},{"question":"You test a model on a free tier. What does the free tier tell you?","options":["How fast your product will feel to its users","The rate limits you will get when you pay","Whether the model can do the task you need","Which paid provider will give you the lowest latency"],"answer":2,"explain":"A free tier shows whether the model can do your task. Free capacity is slower and more rate limited, so measure latency on the tier you will pay for."}]}